			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831561">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Containment procedures, then description of the scp’s and finally interviews addendums and what the foundations future with the scp may hold</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A young man found by the foundation with limited knowledge of most anomalies involving, or labeled as magic. A modern day architect can’t explain exactly how the great pyramids were built, but can gain a basic understanding by examining them, and probably come up with a Rough theory. This scp can do the same with magical/ mythical items. As well as use any gained knowledge to enhance his own ability to make what he calls amateur level anomalies, such as crude malfunctioning versions of existing scps, or his own extremely flawed anomalies (obviously to a certain extent such as not being able to even attempt to replicate meters/ complex humanoids)</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The article shows there interest in his ability to understand the anomalous effects of certain scps, But also the danger he can pose to himself and some people around him, due to his lack of expertise or a mentor. Containment procedures start off easy as they get to know him. But as they realize just how powerful he is the foundation gets stricter and stricter. Finally getting to foam padded rooms, and masks to prevent him from performing magic without heavy supervision. The article will also include the foundations extreme concern of the scp landing in unwanted hands due to its ability to make small scale anomalies. And replicate existing anomalies which is obviously not in the foundations best interests</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The scp’s complete immaturity and lack of expertise or knowledge of just how powerful he can be, make him extremely hard to utilize in any situation. But his ability to gain an understanding on certain anomalies make him extremely useful to the foundation. If they can just keep a 14 year old “amateur witch” as he often labels himself: under control</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> This whole scp is themed around a witch that’s to young to fully understand what there doing. Also for anyone who didn’t get my first my first reference, basically you know 2+2=4 and this scp understands that a tormented soul+ the blood of a virgin+ a specific statue. Could theoretically make an extremely poor copy of scp-173. (Don’t take this example to seriously it’s just an example)</p>

